  "id": "DrugBank_DB11576 - MONDO_1239",
  "verbalization": "Ferric Oxide is associated with Anemia Of Prematurity through a chain of indications that involve Ferrous Gluconate, a common treatment for anemias. The evidence suggests that Ferric Oxide may be used to treat a range of anemias, including Hypochromic, Microcytic, and Deficiency Anemia, all of which are linked to Ferrous Gluconate. This implies that Ferric Oxide may have a broad therapeutic profile that includes the treatment of anemias associated with iron deficiency or other underlying conditions. The consistent association with Ferrous Gluconate and Anemia Of Prematurity suggests a potential mechanism where Ferric Oxide could be used to manage anemias that are responsive to iron supplementation. The evidence supports a pathway where Ferric Oxide may be repurposed to treat anemias, particularly those that are microcytic or hypochromic, by targeting the underlying iron deficiency. The integration of these paths highlights the potential for Ferric Oxide to be a viable treatment option for Anemia Of Prematurity, especially in cases where Ferrous Gluconate is already being used.",
